   "text": {
    "L1": "Science uses evidence, not just opinions, to explain the world.",
    "L2": "When new evidence does not fit an old idea, scientists check it carefully.",
    "L3": "If the evidence holds up, the idea is changed or replaced.",
    "L4": "People once thought Earth was flat. Several observations challenged that idea.",
    "L5": "A ship disappearing hull-first, a round eclipse shadow, and space photos are evidence that Earth is round.",
    "L6": "Changing an idea because of better evidence is a strength of science, not a failure.",
    "L7": "A fair test changes one thing at a time and repeats measurements, so the evidence can be trusted.",
    "L8": "Now choose what should guide a scientific idea."
   },
